<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,425.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,425.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,425 today from 1,415 on Feb 7, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1485    13.479	  1475    13.388</p>
<p>   1a   1492 11300.000	  1478 11194.000</p>
<p>   2    1755    25.071	  1743    24.906</p>
<p>   2a   1833 15029.000	  1812 14863.000</p>
<p>   3    1471    13.571	  1461    13.481</p>
<p>   3a   1469 11593.000	  1451 11450.000</p>
<p>   6    1256    12.950	  1254    12.931</p>
